WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.080
Describe architectural styles using components,
connectors and constraints.

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:08.602
A name alone does not explain behavior or tradeoffs.

00:00:08.602 --> 00:00:14.970
Real systems often combine styles, so identify which
part of the system each description fits.

00:00:14.970 --> 00:00:21.134
Evaluate the assumptions that make an advantage
possible, and use shared vocabulary to make

00:00:21.134 --> 00:00:24.995
decisions easier to inspect rather than to assign
labels.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:29.689
The repository style coordinates components through
shared information.

00:00:29.689 --> 00:00:34.511
It can simplify data management while coupling
clients to a common model.

00:00:34.511 --> 00:00:39.002
Blackboard systems extend the idea through
cooperating computations.

00:00:39.002 --> 00:00:45.607
Examine schema ownership, concurrency and failure
behavior before claiming easy reuse or centralized

00:00:45.607 --> 00:00:51.683
control; one shared box does not automatically
provide scalable or highly available storage.

00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:55.975
Pipes and filters compose transformations through
data contracts.

00:00:55.975 --> 00:01:02.552
A linear pipeline is one specialization, and batch
processing changes when output becomes available.

00:01:02.552 --> 00:01:08.931
Compiler examples show that practical systems often
add shared representations, creating hybrids.

00:01:08.931 --> 00:01:15.245
Consider conversion cost, buffering and feedback
before assuming that connecting reusable stages

00:01:15.245 --> 00:01:20.178
automatically gives good performance or supports
every interaction pattern.

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:25.639
Objects encapsulate state and contracts; layers
organize services by abstraction.

00:01:25.639 --> 00:01:30.138
Both help manage dependencies but do not erase
behavioral coupling.

00:01:30.138 --> 00:01:34.032
Distinguish logical layers from physical deployment
tiers.

00:01:34.032 --> 00:01:40.545
Shared mutable state and changes in interface
meaning can still propagate, so evaluate the actual

00:01:40.545 --> 00:01:46.253
contracts and dependency rules rather than assuming
isolation from the diagram alone.
